AlkylationReagent: iodoacetamide
CellType: O+ erythrocytes
CleavageAgent: Trypsin
CollisionEnergy: 35% normalized collision energy
Compound: Shld-1
Compound: 2.5 nM WR99210
Compound: IBMX (250 muM)
Compound: BAPTA-AM (40 muM)
Compound: 8Br-cAMP (100 muM)
Compound: PKI (20 muM)
DevelopmentalStage: late schizont
Disease: malaria
EnrichmentMethod: TiO2 based enrichment of phosphopeptides
FlowRateChromatogram: 1 ml flow rate per minute
FractionationMethod: fractionated on Xbridge C18 5 um 250 x 4.6 mm column (Waters Corporation, Milford, MA, USA) using Agilent 1100 binary pump (Agilent Technologies, Santa Clara, CA, USA).
FractionationMethod: The sample was resolved through reverse-phase liquid chromatography method using a gradient of 5 to 60% solvent B (10 mM triethylammonium bicarbonate, pH 8.5 in 95% Acetonitrile) with 1 ml flow rate per minute for over 60 min.
FragmentMassTolerance: 0.1 Da
FragmentationMethod: higher-energy collisional dissociation (HCD)
GeneticModification: PfCDPK1 locus with 3HA-DD
Genotype: PfCDPK1-3HA-DD parasites
GradientTime: over 60 min
GradientTime: over 120 min
Instrument: Orbitrap Fusion Tribrid mass spectrometer
Label: iTRAQ labeling
MaterialType: cells
Modification: Oxidation of methionine
Modification: phosphorylation of serine, threonine and tyrosine
NumberOfBiologicalReplicates: 4
NumberOfFractions: A total of 96 fractions were concatenated into 12 fractions
NumberOfMissedCleavages: one
NumberOfSamples: four samples
NumberOfTechnicalReplicates: technical duplicates
Organism: Plasmodium falciparum
PooledSample: pooled
PrecursorMassTolerance: 20 ppm
ReductionReagent: DTT
Separation: Peptides were resolved on an analytical column (75 micro x 15 cm, 3 micro particle and 100 Aa pore size) using a linear gradient of 7 to 30% of solvent B (0.1% formic acid in 95% Acetonitrile) over 120 min.
Temperature: 37 degreesC
